# ic15_continuous_prism.lgi
# interpolate / continuous of the LINEAR field flin = 1 + 2x - 3y +
# 0.5z from a prism mesh (a 5 x 5 triangle grid through 4 layers).
# Each prism is split into 14 tets around its median (cinterpolate_elem,
# Oct 2026), so a linear field is exact. Before that, every value was
# wrong (up to 106 off on a unit cube): the prism branch was a copy of
# the hex branch and read vertices 7 and 8, which a prism does not have.
# check: linear | out_ic15.inp | fc
read / avs / src_prism.inp / mo_src
read / avs / sink_points.inp / mo_snk
cmo / addatt / mo_snk / fc / VDOUBLE / scalar / nnodes
interpolate / continuous / mo_snk fc / 1,0,0 / mo_src flin
dump / avs / out_ic15.inp / mo_snk
finish
